  "summary": "An artistic tradition featuring intricate geometric and floral motifs used in carving and textile design",
  "description": "Okir art features flowing geometric patterns, arabesque designs, and stylized natural elements like the naga (dragon) and sarimanok (mythical bird), created through wood carving and textile weaving. These motifs reflect the Maranao's Islamic faith and their sophisticated cultural heritage, with designs symbolizing prosperity, protection, and cosmic harmony.",
